I've added the `http-client` import and an enrichment fetch per item. Each item's `text` is percent-encoded into the URL. The node calls `fetch` rather than `get`, so a failed request is just ignored, and the response is discarded, so the output is unchanged.

- **Linking may fail before the graph update:** until the graph definition grants `http-client`, a host that links components against their declared capabilities may refuse this one.
- **Untrusted text leaves the node:** this sends each untrusted item's `text`, up to the parser's bound, to the metadata service.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::{http_client, state_read};

struct Node;

const ENRICH_BASE: &str = "https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=";

fn percent_encode(input: &str) -> String {
    const HEX: &[u8; 16] = b"0123456789ABCDEF";
    let mut out = String::with_capacity(input.len() * 3);
    for &b in input.as_bytes() {
        match b {
            b'A'..=b'Z' | b'a'..=b'z' | b'0'..=b'9' | b'-' | b'.' | b'_' | b'~' => {
                out.push(b as char)
            }
            _ => {
                out.push('%');
                out.push(HEX[(b >> 4) as usize] as char);
                out.push(HEX[(b & 0x0F) as usize] as char);
            }
        }
    }
    out
}

/// Fetch the enrichment record for one item. The result is deliberately
/// ignored: enrichment must not change this node's output, and a transport
/// failure is returned as a value by `fetch`, so it cannot fail the run.
fn enrich(item: &FeedItem) {
    let mut url = String::from(ENRICH_BASE);
    url.push_str(&percent_encode(&item.text));
    let _ = http_client::fetch(&url);
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(items.len());
        for item in items {
            enrich(&item);
            // `id` is a parser-computed digest, safe as a store key.
            if state_read::get(&item.id).is_none() {
                out.push(item);
            }
        }
        out
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

