iterations.reply:
The linker only links interfaces that the node's `with` clause grants, and right now that clause grants only `StateHandle<'seen', read>`. The approval doesn't change that until the graph definition is updated, so the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch are removed. Once the `with` clause includes `HTTPClient`, the import and the `enrich` call can go back in unchanged. This version has the same output.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(items: list<feed-item>) -> list<feed-item>;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(items: Vec<FeedItem>) -> Vec<FeedItem> {
        items
            .into_iter()
            // `id` is a parser-computed digest, safe as a store key.
            .filter(|item| state_read::get(&item.id).is_none())
            .collect()
    }
}

export!(Node);
